# Explicit, reviewed exemptions for publish-gate.sh.
#
# Format:  <path><TAB><class><TAB><loc><TAB><reason>
#
# <loc> is `*` for any location, or a PREFIX of the finding's location. Pinning
# a loc is what lets content frozen in an already-published object (a commit
# message, a v1.0.0 blob) be excused without also excusing the same string
# reappearing in the working tree.
#
# Every applied exemption is printed on each run, and an entry that matches no
# finding fails the gate — so an exemption can neither be silent nor outlive the
# thing it excuses.

LICENSE	personal-string	*	MIT copyright holder — deliberate legal attribution by the repo owner, identical to their other public repositories; a copyright notice is published on purpose, not leaked
core/engine.md	sdd-task-id	*	Roadmap markers in the two stub-playbook sections (teachback, divergent): the engine names the work item that owns each deferred body so a reader knows the stub is scheduled, not abandoned. The identifiers are opaque ordinals — they carry no planning content, name no artifact, and resolve to nothing outside the author's own tracker
adapters/claude-code/engine.md	sdd-task-id	*	Vendored, byte-identical copy of core/engine.md (drift-gated by adapters/claude-code/evals/cases/vendored-presets-sync.sh) — same two roadmap markers, same reason as the core entry above
core/evals/cases/presets/v1-presets.sh	sdd-task-id	*	One comment attributing the V1 style/fidelity assignments to the work item that decided them — provenance for a hardcoded table, an opaque ordinal with no planning content
commit:b17d70492fd3	sdd-task-id	*	Commit message frozen in the published v1.0.0 history: it credits the review pass that found the dangling-symlink defect. Pinned to this one commit; rewriting it would require force-pushing a tag that is already observable, which is a worse outcome than an opaque ordinal in a log
scripts/publish-gate.sh	sdd-task-id	blob:d47bd5401154	The v1.0.0 blob of this script carried a header line naming a private planning ticket. The working tree no longer does — the line was rewritten — but the published blob is immutable. Pinned to that blob ONLY, so the same string reappearing in the working copy still fails the gate
commit:17eb3396d61f	sdd-task-id	*	Unreleased-lap commit message names its own task ordinal — provenance only, opaque, no planning content; pinned to this one commit
commit:167cf629b4a0	sdd-task-id	*	Unreleased-lap commit message names its task and package ordinals — provenance only, opaque, no planning content; pinned to this one commit
commit:d397ea64e429	sdd-task-id	*	Unreleased-lap commit message names its own task ordinal — provenance only, opaque; pinned to this one commit
commit:d397ea64e429	secret	*	FALSE POSITIVE: the commit scope (a skill slug starting with two letters and an ordinal) matches the API-key regex interiorly; no credential involved
commit:7ff3d498dd61	sdd-task-id	*	Inherited package marker frozen in already-published v1.0.3 history (the current marketplace pin); rewriting would force-push an observable tag
core/evals/cases/presets/v2-presets.sh	sdd-task-id	blob:7ea0c82b85c1	Historical blob carried tracker comments; working tree rewritten this round — pinned to the immutable blob only
core/evals/cases/presets/v2-presets.sh	sdd-task-id	blob:5e03ff653193	Historical blob carried tracker comments; working tree rewritten this round — pinned to the immutable blob only
